module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode

// ONE ROW PER FAILURE CLASS, BECAUSE ONE SENTENCE PER FLEET WAS THE DEFECT.
//
// These classes lived in a single 11,751-character `p(text:)` blob in gunbc.design_document. Every
// lane that named a new class appended to that one line, so two lanes naming two UNRELATED classes
// collided on every merge -- five conflict cycles on one PR in one night, every resolution purely
// additive, zero sentences ever lost. That is textual contention standing in for semantic
// contention: the classes are independent, and only the line was shared. Split into rows, two lanes
// touch two declarations and never collide, while two lanes editing the SAME class still conflict --
// which is correct, because that is real disagreement about one fact (DESIGN section 2).
//
// THIS CUT IS MECHANICAL AND ITS ORACLE IS AN EMPTY DIFF. Each row carries its authored sentence
// BYTE-FOR-BYTE and the projection renders them in roster order, so regenerating DESIGN.md after the
// split produces no change at all. Sorting the rows by identity would reorder the paragraph and
// destroy that oracle -- a projection defect would then be indistinguishable from an intended edit --
// so order is carried by the roster and determinism comes from the roster being source-ordered.
//
// WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: the analytic fields (misleading surface, actual question, failure
// mechanism, required guard) that these rows will eventually carry. Filling them for seventeen
// classes means authoring analysis that does not exist in the text today, which is semantic
// rewriting inside a structural cut and has no oracle. They land in a follow-up where each class is
// a readable diff.
//
// WHY `evidence` STAYS EMPTY ON EVERY ROW, recorded so the next author does not fill in seventeen
// empty lists and call it citation hygiene. The field is a typed `DeclarationRef` list and a typed
// citation is genuinely better than a symbol spelled inside `authored` -- but measured today,
// nothing resolves it and nobody reads it. `v2.lens.cited_symbol_resolution` takes its population
// from `hand_authored_production_doc_declaration_refs` (HandAuthoredDocBind primary_work plus
// additional_works) and this carrier is not in it; `gunbc.design_document` projects `.authored`
// alone, so a populated `evidence` renders nowhere; and that lens has not executed on a push since
// the 2026-08-23 directive deleted its job, which its own `cited_symbol_required_check_note`
// records as a declared rung drop to mitigatable. A citation that no resolver covers and no reader
// sees is not partial coverage -- it is the decoration DESIGN section 4b calls worse than absent,
// because it will be cited as coverage. THE OCCASION MATTERS: this was decided in the diff that
// repaired a specimen whose whole defect was three symbols nothing ever checked, and populating an
// unchecked field there would have reproduced the finding inside its own repair.
// dissolve-on: the cited-symbol law's own trigger -- enrollment widens to every structural
// DeclarationRef carrier when the Node-tree reader lands. At that point these rows carry resolvable
// evidence and the symbols in `authored` become the redundant half.
//
// WHY A ROW IS A LIST OF RECEIPTS, AND THE TWO REPAIRS THIS SUPERSEDES.
//
// FIRST REPAIR, blob to rows: these classes lived in one 11,751-character `p(text:)` blob and every
// lane appending collided -- five conflict cycles on one PR in one night. Split into `data` rows.
// SECOND REPAIR, rows to one line each: that split left a shared BLOCK TAIL, `evidence: [],` then
// `}`, which a three-way merge factored out of the conflict region -- one tail below the markers for
// two half-blocks above -- so the additive resolution yielded a first block whose closing lines
// belonged to the second. Measured with `git merge-file` at merge base d0009ca531.
//
// BOTH REPAIRS MEASURED ONLY THE APPEND OF A WHOLE ROW, and both rested on one premise, stated in
// the first: that two lanes editing the SAME class conflicting is "correct, because that is real
// disagreement about one fact." THAT PREMISE IS FALSE FOR THIS CARRIER, and it is why nobody looked
// inside a row for two repairs -- it made intra-row contention look correct, so it was never
// measured. What accretes on a class is INDEPENDENT RECEIPTS from unrelated lanes, not competing
// claims about one fact: on 2026-09-02/03 three lanes appended three independent receipts to
// `state_space_conflation` and resolved it by hand-negotiating byte order, and one row reached
// 23,023 characters. Independent accretion is not disagreement. The class is filed as
// `premise_that_a_shared_subject_means_disagreement`.
//
// SO THE RECEIPTS ARE MODELLED AS SEVERABLE PARTS -- SEVERABLE, NOT TYPED; see the classification
// paragraph below, which is the honest limit of what this buys. Two lanes amending two receipts now
// touch two line regions with an unchanged line between them, which is what a three-way merge needs.
// MEASURED on this carrier's own `state_space_conflation` with `git merge-file`, base/ours/theirs:
// two lanes EDITING different receipts -> 0 conflicts; two lanes APPENDING a receipt -> 1 conflict.
//
// THE APPEND CASE IS NOT ZERO AND MUST NOT BE READ AS ZERO. Two lanes appending still collide,
// because both insert at the same point. What changed is the SHAPE: the region holds one whole list
// element per side, the `],` / `evidence: [],` / `}` tail stays OUTSIDE it rather than being factored
// in, and the additive resolution is total. Before this change the same collision presented as two
// 23,023-character lines and was resolved by negotiating byte order by hand. This makes survivors
// safely resolvable; it does not remove them.
//
// EVERY ELEMENT CARRIES A TRAILING COMMA, INCLUDING THE LAST, AND THIS IS LOAD-BEARING RATHER THAN
// STYLE. Without it, appending a receipt must also add a comma to the previous line, which drags the
// preceding receipt into the conflict region and destroys the minimality measured above. A
// reformatter that "tidies" the final comma away silently restores the worse geometry. Nothing
// enforces this; it is the one property here held by this paragraph.
//
// TEN ROWS CARRIED `authored: "..." as NonEmptyStr`, a cast on a field declared `String`, dropped
// here because a list has no such cast. Recorded rather than silently removed: the cast bought
// nothing, and its presence on ten rows and absence on seventy-one is the kind of drift a per-part
// declaration makes visible. Those counts are read off the derivation base named in the PR body; they are a
// dated observation about that tree, not an invariant.
//
// THE RECEIPTS ARE STILL `String` AND THAT IS AN OPEN SECTION 4c GAP, NAMED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT
// FOR A READER TO DISCOVER. Section 4c says any invariant, receipt, ruling, citation, status, count
// or dissolution condition belongs in a typed carrier, and a `List<String>` element still mixes all
// of those inside one prose blob. THIS CHANGE NEITHER CREATES NOR REPAIRS THAT: the field it
// replaces was `authored: String`, one larger blob of exactly the same unclassified prose, so the
// classification rung is unmoved and only the merge geometry improved. Saying the parts are TYPED
// would be the section 4b(1) inflation this file already warns about one paragraph down, which is
// why the wording above says SEVERABLE.
//
// WHY CLASSIFICATION IS NOT DONE HERE, since a gap named without a reason is just an excuse. The
// carrier holds 1,837 receipts across 83 rows; classifying them is an authored judgement per
// receipt, not a derivation, so it cannot ride in on a re-derivation the way this split does and it
// cannot be verified by the content-hash identity that makes this change safe. Attempting both at
// once would give up the one property that lets this land at all: that every carried byte is
// provably unchanged. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability rather than an artifact: a receipt variant
// model whose constructors cover the kinds section 4c enumerates, sufficient for an EXHAUSTIVE
// match over a row's parts -- at which point an unclassified receipt has no constructor and the
// prose cannot be written, which is rung 4 rather than a lens. THE SPLIT IS WHAT MAKES THAT
// AFFORDABLE: classifying a row becomes an edit to one file that conflicts with nobody, where
// today it is an edit to a shared blob that collides with every concurrent lane.
//
// THE RUNG, STATED HONESTLY BECAUSE THIS PARAGRAPH IS WHAT THE NEXT APPENDER READS. The population
// carries no severable tail. The SHAPE IS NOT ENFORCED -- no lens covers row shape on this carrier
// -- so one hand-authored multi-line row restores the two-line tail and the whole geometry with it.
// The invalid state therefore stays WRITABLE and this is mechanically preventable at best, not
// structural; calling the shape construction would be the rung inflation DESIGN section 4b(1) names,
// sitting in the annotation an author consults before appending. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as the
// capability and not as an artifact that would contribute to one: a row-shape obligation DECIDED for
// every declaration of a growth-surface type rather than observed on the rows that happen to exist
// -- the corpus already reads declared types per declaration through `v2.std.decl_index`
// `data_decl_type_facts`, and what is missing is a producer carrying each declaration's source
// EXTENT, sufficient for refusing a multi-line row of such a type at authoring time. Until that
// exists, the shape is a convention held by review and by this paragraph.
//
// THE LOSS STATES ARE MEASURED AND THE SET IS COMPLETE, which is why no check is written here.
// Against a gunbc built from source at d0009ca531, severing a multi-line row is loud in every one of
// the three ways the two-line tail can be cut: losing BOTH lines and losing `}` alone are PARSE
// refusals at the module index (`expected expression, found Eq` -- a `data` keyword landing in
// record-field position), and losing `evidence: [],` alone is a RESOLVE refusal (`missing required
// field 'evidence' in literal of type 'RecurringFailureMode'`). Nothing silent was found in that
// set. A brace-balance or declared-versus-rostered check would be the DESIGN section 4b decoration:
// permanently green, because the only corpus it could fire on never reaches it.
//
// A THIRD CONSEQUENCE NOBODY ARGUED FOR IN ADVANCE, appended by a later lane rather than authored
// here: THE SPLIT MADE A QUESTION DECIDABLE THAT WAS PREVIOUSLY ONLY SEARCHABLE. This cut was
// justified on merge geometry, and then on making a duplicate declaration unwritable because two
// files cannot share a name. But the question a lane most often needs to answer about a contended
// carrier is "which identities do I add?" -- and under the blob that was a substring search inside
// an 11,751-character line, which is how two duplicate declarations hid in plain sight for two hours
// on 2026-09-03 while three separate instruments read the file and reported clean. After the split
// it is a set difference over filenames against the roster directory, and it returns an EMPTY RESULT
// A READER CAN TRUST. A SET DIFFERENCE OVER FILENAMES HAS A MEANING; A GREP INSIDE A MEGA-LINE HAS A
// HIT COUNT. The occasion was a parked branch carrying 83 stale declarations of this shape: the
// emptiness of its own contribution was decidable in one command, and that is what made the
// resolution safe to perform without its author.
//
// AN UNPREDICTED BENEFIT IS WORTH MORE IN THIS RECORD THAN A PREDICTED ONE, because it is evidence
// the cut fell at a real joint rather than at a convenient one.
//
// AND THE SHARED-BLOCK-TAIL GEOMETRY ABOVE IS NOT A PROPERTY OF THIS CARRIER, OR OF `.dag` AT ALL.
// The SECOND REPAIR paragraph measures it on rows -- a block whose `evidence: [],` / `}` tail is
// factored out of the conflict region, so an additive resolution yields a first block whose closing
// lines belong to the second. On 2026-09-03 the IDENTICAL geometry appeared in Rust, in
// `v1_compiler.cli_run`, merging gunbc#10267 into gunbc#9725: both sides appended a `pub fn` at one
// insertion point, BOTH BODIES WERE TRUNCATED AT THE MARKERS, and the single closing brace sat below
// the region, shared. It is a property of ANY three-way merge where a block's tail is factored out,
// and brace-delimited languages are exposed exactly as row files are.
//
// THE RUST FORM IS WORSE THAN THE ROW FORM, WHICH IS WHY IT IS RECORDED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT AS AN
// ANECDOTE. Two row-bodies above one tail fail loudly -- the loss states are measured above and every
// one of them is a parse or resolve refusal. Two FUNCTION bodies above one brace need not fail at
// all: the outcome can be a function that SWALLOWED THE OTHER'S SIGNATURE AND COMPILED. A silently
// wrong merge that typechecks is the artifact DESIGN section 5 ranks worst, and the reflexive
// additive resolution is precisely what produces it.
//
// THE READ THAT CATCHES IT COSTS NOTHING: before unioning, look at the LAST line of each side and the
// line immediately AFTER the closing marker. If neither side closes itself and the text below supplies
// the closer, the union needs one inserted between them.

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr, List }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef }
import v2.std.algebra { fold_list }

type RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: NonEmptyStr
  receipts: List<String>
  evidence: List<DeclarationRef>
}

// THE RECEIPTS ARE THE ROW'S PARTS AND THE JOIN IS RENDERING, WHICH IS WHY THIS FOLD LIVES HERE.
// Concatenation with no separator is exact: each receipt carries its own trailing space, so this
// reproduces the single string it replaced BYTE FOR BYTE, and that identity is the oracle the
// decomposition was checked against rather than a claim about it.
fn authored(r: RecurringFailureMode) -> String {
  fold_list(xs: r.receipts, empty: "", cons: fn(acc, receipt) { concat(acc, receipt) })
}
